Rule 1 (cross product requires dimension size 3)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≠ 3 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) ≠ 3
>>
Rule 2 (cross product requires same number of dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≠ ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 4 (cross product requires dimension size 3 for both inputs)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= shape(v_1, 0) ≠ 3 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) ≠ 3
>>
Rule 6 (dimension must be valid)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int} |= v_3 ≥ ndim(v_1) ∧ v_3 ≤ ndim(v_2)
